 "_comment": "ITEM ICONS for the common SRD/BG3 gear that actually appears in Inventory / Market / Forge (EPIC D). The bg3.wiki lead/infobox image of an item page IS its icon (verified across weapons & armour). Scope uses the colon form 'item:<slug>' to mirror the class:/race: convention; the viewer's _safe_scope writes it as item_<slug> and the /image?scope= endpoint's _scope_key normalises BOTH the UI's request ('item-<slug>') AND this slug to the same key, so an icon resolves only when the slug matches the item NAME the engine grants. The slug is the engine/SRD item name lowercased with non-alnum -> '-' (e.g. 'Chain Mail' -> item:chain-mail, 'Studded Leather Armor' -> item:studded-leather-armor), EXACTLY the screens' slug() helper. The 'title' is the bg3.wiki page to fetch (BG3 uses British 'Armour' / plural shop names, so title often differs from the scope slug). LICENSING IS LOAD-BEARING: official Larian/WotC item icons are © -> they land ONLY in gitignored content/worlds/_private/<world>/images/ and are NEVER committed; scripts/license_check.py must stay green. Re-run: python3 tools/ingest/wiki_images.py tools/ingest/manifest_images_items.json",
